From a9b5107af4d802627a5fede7215161c5ac725bec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 02:43:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ga2: mouse play, long DMA chains, stall diagnostics

- Mouse (ps2_mouse, ps2_mouse_menus): left click = Circle, right = Cross,
  middle = Select, wheel = Up/Down; an on-screen pad (D-pad, face buttons,
  L1/L2/R1/R2, Select, Start) appears in the side bars while the mouse moves
  (over the picture edges only near them when there are no bars). Known menus
  follow the pointer: hovering an item moves the game's cursor there with
  D-pad presses, clicking also confirms. Zettai and Mugen title menus are
  mapped (menu object found by its type word, cursor byte, item rects).
- Without a gamepad the D-pad also tilts the left stick fully (the ship map
  scrolls only with the stick).
- The game window opens 16:9 so the 4:3 picture leaves bars for the pad.
- DMA chains may run to 2^20 tags: Mugen's tutorial battle sends 4000+ tag
  VIF1 chains; the 4096 cap left the chain unfinished and the game waiting
  forever for its completion. A cut chain is now reported.
- Diagnostics: GA2_PERF also prints each guest thread's resume pc/ra and the
  VIF1/GIF/D_STAT state; GA2_RAM_DUMP_DIR + F12 writes EE RAM;
  GA2_VU1CAP_ONLY=<hash,...> samples only those code images.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
